    "raw": "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 14.061 + 0.476 \\times 10^{-3} T - 1.807 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{\\circ}-H_{298}^{\\circ}=14.061\\times10^{-3}T+0.238\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+1.807\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-4.820$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-2000 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -1.572 + 0.995 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.774 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} - 109.100 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -1.572 - 0.995 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.774 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} - 54.550 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 0.145 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Wagman (126). Other data from Sommer (110). ",
